From e33a85f323352adac943738516f984a2c19b265b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: blizz <blizz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 23:46:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] A session can run a program Android runs itself
 (bionic_command, bionic_env, bionic_dir)

An ARM64 game runs in an Android-native (bionic) Wine, started through
/system/bin/linker64 with its own environment, without Box64 or the
glibc rootfs. The game screen starts that command in place of
GuestProgramLauncherComponent when the intent carries bionic_command
({screen} becomes the screen's size), bionic_env (NAME=value, over the
session's own variables) and bionic_dir (its folder). The X server,
shared memory and sound servers are the same as for every other game.
---
